</figure>
</section>
<section id="S6.SS2.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Number of selected senses during training <math id="S6.SS2.SSS0.Px2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math></h4>

<div id="S6.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#S6.T5" title="Table 5 ‣ Number of clusters 𝑘 ‣ 6.2. Sense Selections ‣ 6. Ablation Studies ‣ Decoder-based Sense Knowledge Distillation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> shows the impact of varying <math id="S6.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math> for semantic consistency. When <math id="S6.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa=1</annotation></semantics></math>, performance is consistently lower, indicating that an insufficient weight on the sense-level objective limits the effectiveness of DSKD. Increasing <math id="S6.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math> generally improves performance, but larger values do not necessarily lead to further improvements. Based on this observation, we select <math id="S6.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa=5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa=5</annotation></semantics></math> as a balanced setting that yields strong performance across tasks and backbones.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S6.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">6.3. </span>Training Hyperparameters</h3>

<section id="S6.SS3.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">DSKD loss coefficient <math id="S6.SS3.SSS0.Px1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{p}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.SS3.SSS0.Px1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{n}</annotation></semantics></math></h4>

<div id="S6.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#S6.T5" title="Table 5 ‣ Number of clusters 𝑘 ‣ 6.2. Sense Selections ‣ 6. Ablation Studies ‣ Decoder-based Sense Knowledge Distillation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> reports the performance under different values of <math id="S6.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{p}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, where we tie the two coefficients. Overall, the results indicate that the choice of <math id="S6.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> plays a non-trivial role in balancing the contribution of sense-level supervision. When <math id="S6.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> is set too small, the effect of DSKD becomes marginal and the performance approaches that of standard KD, suggesting insufficient utilization of sense information. In contrast, overly large values of <math id="S6.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> do not yield further improvements and may even hurt performance, as the sense-level objective begins to dominate the training process. Based on this trade-off, we select <math id="S6.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=1.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1.0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=1.0</annotation></semantics></math> for LLaMA-based models and <math id="S6.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=1.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=1.5</annotation></semantics></math> for Mistral-based models, which consistently achieve strong performance.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S6.T6" class="ltx_table">
<table id="S6.T6.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="S6.T6.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S6.T6.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_th_row ltx_border_l ltx_border_r ltx_border_t"><math id="S6.T6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{p}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S6.T6.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">, <math id="S6.T6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{n}</annotation></semantics></math></span></th>
<th id="S6.T6.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_r ltx_border_t" colspan="2"><span id="S6.T6.2.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">LLaMA</span></th>
<th id="S6.T6.2.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_r ltx_border_t" colspan="2"><span id="S6.T6.2.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Mistral</span></th></tr>
<tr id="S6.T6.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S6.T6.2.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_th_row ltx_border_l ltx_border_r"></th>
