<section id="Ax1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix">Appendix</h2>

</section>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Open Source Code</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We will release our project, including the training code, sense dictionary, and model weights, as open source project on GitHub after the review period. The implementation is built with NumPy <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib35" title="" class="ltx_ref">Harris et al., 2020</a>)</cite>, PyTorch <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib36" title="" class="ltx_ref">Paszke et al., 2019</a>)</cite>, and scikit-learn <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib34" title="" class="ltx_ref">Pedregosa et al., 2011</a>)</cite> for data processing and model training, with Matplotlib <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib37" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hunter, 2007</a>)</cite> used for visualization.
We use Llama-3-8B-Instruct <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">Dubey et al., 2024</a>)</cite> and Mistral-7B-Instruct <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">Jiang et al., 2023</a>)</cite> as the teacher models. We obtained research licenses for both models from Hugging Face and downloaded them using the <span id="A1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">transformers</span> library <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib38" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wolf et al., 2020</a>)</cite>. All evaluation benchmarks are accessed through the Hugging Face <span id="A1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">datasets</span> library <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib39" title="" class="ltx_ref">Lhoest et al., 2021</a>)</cite>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Dataset</h2>

<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1. </span>Dictionary and Thesauri</h3>

<div id="A2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We build the sense dictionary from the Wikipedia dump <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib30" title="" class="ltx_ref">WikipediaCorpus, 2024</a>)</cite> and the training dataset. We construct the relationship dictionary using synonym and antonym pairs extracted from Wiktionary <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib29" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ylonen, 2022</a>)</cite> and Roget’s Thesaurus through HG2Vec <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">McCutcheon, 2010</a>; <a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wang and Zaki, 2022</a>)</cite>. To incorporate morphological information, we also integrate semantic root forms obtained from MorphoLEX-English <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib31" title="" class="ltx_ref">Sánchez-Gutiérrez et al., 2018</a>)</cite>. Table <a href="#A2.T8" title="Table 8 ‣ B.1. Dictionary and Thesauri ‣ Appendix B Dataset ‣ Decoder-based Sense Knowledge Distillation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a> summarizes the statistics of the dictionaries used in our experiments.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A2.T8" class="ltx_table">
<div id="A2.T8.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:345.0pt;height:88.5pt;vertical-align:-41.7pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(2.4pt,-0.6pt) scale(1.01436495706161,1.01436495706161) ;">
<table id="A2.T8.2.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="A2.T8.2.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A2.T8.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_th_row ltx_border_l ltx_border_r ltx_border_t"></th>
<th id="A2.T8.2.1.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_r ltx_border_t"><span id="A2.T8.2.1.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Llama-3-8B-Instruct</span></th>
<th id="A2.T8.2.1.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_r ltx_border_t"><span id="A2.T8.2.1.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Mistral-7B-Instruct</span></th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="A2.T8.2.1.2" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A2.T8.2.1.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_l ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">Tokenizer vocab size</th>
<td id="A2.T8.2.1.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">128,256</td>
