<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Model Comparison: Space/Parameters and Time</h2>

<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Tables <a href="#A4.T11" title="Table 11 ‣ Appendix D Model Comparison: Space/Parameters and Time ‣ Decoder-based Sense Knowledge Distillation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a> and <a href="#A4.T12" title="Table 12 ‣ Appendix D Model Comparison: Space/Parameters and Time ‣ Decoder-based Sense Knowledge Distillation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a> provide additional comparisons of model efficiency in terms of parameter size, memory usage, training time, and evaluation latency. Table <a href="#A4.T11" title="Table 11 ‣ Appendix D Model Comparison: Space/Parameters and Time ‣ Decoder-based Sense Knowledge Distillation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a>summarizes the space and training-time cost of the teacher models and their corresponding student variants under KD and DSKD, showing that DSKD introduces only a marginal increase in training time while preserving the same memory footprint as KD. Table <a href="#A4.T12" title="Table 12 ‣ Appendix D Model Comparison: Space/Parameters and Time ‣ Decoder-based Sense Knowledge Distillation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a> further reports evaluation time across different benchmarks, where KD and DSKD exhibit nearly identical inference latency, indicating that the proposed sense-level supervision does not introduce additional runtime overhead during evaluation.</p>
</div>
